## Installation

### As a built-in plugin

1. Copy this directory into `plugins/{{.PluginID}}/`
2. Copy the Go source into `internal/plugin/builtin/{{.PackageName}}/`
3. Add an import to `internal/plugin/allplugins/allplugins.go`:
   ```go
   _ "github.com/hollis-labs/conduit/internal/plugin/builtin/{{.PackageName}}"
   ```
4. Rebuild: `go install ./cmd/conduit/`

### From Git

```bash
conduit plugin install {{.PluginID}}
```

## Development

- `plugin.yaml` — plugin manifest (name, version, config, registered components)
- `plugin.go` — Go implementation of the Plugin interface
{{- if .WithAgent}}
- `agents/{{.PluginID}}.yaml` — agent profile
{{- end}}
{{- if .Envelopes}}
- `ui/` — React envelope components
{{- end}}

## Plugin Lifecycle

1. `init()` registers the constructor in the plugin registry
2. `Load()` is called when the host discovers and loads the plugin
3. `Unload()` is called on shutdown or when the plugin is disabled
